  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1241 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nThe first full week of October will feature temperatures more \nlike that of early September. Highs will climb into the mid to \nupper 80s on Tuesday and into the upper 80s to lower 90s on \nWednesday and Thursday. Models continue to show an upper level \ndisturbance over the Big Bend/west Texas on Friday and Saturday, \nwith the operational GFS being wetter compared to the ECWMF. Given\nthe uncertainty in the strength of the disturbance will keep PoPs\ncapped in the 20-30% range and confined to the northern Edwards \nPlateau. Otherwise, will carry a dry forecast for next weekend, \nwith temperatures continuing to run above normal for October.",
